edition ObjectiveBend 1
# A resident that faults after its first reply (scenario E of the native activity
# acceptance). Its first await is ordinary; after the reply it yields a second await
# whose patience no deployment admits (the kernel's bound is maxPatience). That is a
# fault of the resumed program itself, which every later delivery would meet again,
# so the delivery commits the activity `faulted` and returns its unused escrow
# (Kernel/ObjectiveActivity.programFault, resumedSegment_never_refuses_program_fault)
# instead of refusing and wedging the await with its escrow locked.
import ./Tally.obend as Tally
def impatient(start: Tally.Start) -> Activity<Tally.Plan, Tally.Resumed, Nat>:
  match perform(Tally.Plan.await({write: {total: start.init}, on: Tally.Source.reply({decider: start.decider}), patience: 4n})):
    case resumed(_):
      match perform(Tally.Plan.await({write: {total: Tally.EditNat.keep()}, on: Tally.Source.reply({decider: start.decider}), patience: 1000000n})):
        case resumed(again): again.view.state.total
